Subject: [PATCH] build: declare the Debian dependencies of debuginfo, kunit and uapi
Origin: other, Peios catalogue qualification review
Upstream-Status: Pending [Debian reference dependency lists]

Three more Debian-rung omissions, found by reading every remaining target's
script against both of its dependency lists after build:debuginfo stopped the
first full release on the Debian rung:

    ./build/make-debuginfo.sh: line 25: make: command not found

- build.debuginfo runs `make kernelrelease`. Natively it gets make from
  dev.peios.build-essentials; its apt list named only binutils, debugedit and
  cpio.
- test.kunit boots the kernel under qemu-system-x86_64 and exits if it is
  absent, but declared no dependencies on either rung. test.modsig, test.fwsig
  and test.stratafs already declare qemu-system-x86 on apt.
- test.uapi compiles the PKM UAPI headers with an ordinary `cc` against the
  libc's /usr/include/linux, and likewise declared nothing.

Debian only. The native test stages cannot run until Peios packages QEMU
(PEI-534), which also covers giving test.kunit its native dependency block.

diff --git a/pekit.toml b/pekit.toml
index 7273cc7..16ad338 100644
--- a/pekit.toml
+++ b/pekit.toml
@@ -323,6 +323,7 @@ command = """
 binutils = "*"
 debugedit = "*"
 cpio = "*"
+build-essential = "*"
 
 # In-tree userspace tooling (perf, bpftool, cpupower, turbostat, rtla, rv). These
 # are userspace ELF programs that live under tools/ in the kernel source, so they
@@ -448,6 +449,13 @@ command = """
 ./build/test-kunit.sh "$PEKIT_KUNIT_OUT"
 """
 
+[test.kunit.dependencies.apt]
+bash            = "*"
+coreutils       = "*"
+grep            = "*"
+sed             = "*"
+qemu-system-x86 = "*"
+
 # Boot the same KACS-enabled kernel with a purpose-built initramfs and exercise
 # StrataFS through real mount/open/read/write/mmap/xattr/link/rename syscalls.
 # Prove the module-signing chain on the modular kernel: boot it with a minimal
@@ -635,3 +643,10 @@ gate = true
 command = """
 bash uapi/check-userspace-clean.sh
 """
+
+# An ordinary userspace compiler and the libc's Linux UAPI headers, which is
+# precisely the environment the check asserts the PKM headers compile in.
+[test.uapi.dependencies.apt]
+bash            = "*"
+grep            = "*"
+build-essential = "*"
